# Remote support log sink (BRC-CLOUD)

Devices POST session logs to BRC-CLOUD. **Do not ask the user to paste logs** when
the upload URL / bucket is known — fetch `/latest` (and the bucket index) first.

## Triage with Jev first, not by hand

`npm run triage [phone|android|desktop|<bucket>]` pulls the bucket, derives the
facts in code (freeze counts by active wallet layer, blocked milliseconds,
grouped error families, how often each family coincides with an *unexplained*
freeze), then asks Jev — TypeSafe System One — for the judgments: user-visible
freeze, primary driver, custody at risk, regression against the previous
session, severity.

```bash
npm run triage android          # verdict
npm run triage android -- --state   # just the extracted facts, no model call
npm run triage android -- --json    # facts + raw answers
```

Read a log by hand only to confirm something the triage flags. Never ask the
model to count — counting, grouping and correlation stay in
`scripts/triage-logs.mjs`. Needs `JEV_API_KEY` in `HANDCASH-DESKTOP/.env`.

## Endpoints

| | |
|---|---|
| Base | `https://brc-cloud.bcryderman.workers.dev` |
| Bucket index | `GET /v1/logs/<bucket>` |
| Latest upload | `GET /v1/logs/<bucket>/latest` |
| Last few | `GET /v1/logs/<bucket>/all` |

Current lab phone bucket (Android): `hc-2c00efc3249a742845a7`

```bash
curl -sS -A "Mozilla/5.0" \
  "https://brc-cloud.bcryderman.workers.dev/v1/logs/hc-2c00efc3249a742845a7/latest"
```

In-app: Settings → Upload URL (`handcash.logs.uploadUrl`). New installs
auto-provision `https://brc-cloud.bcryderman.workers.dev/v1/logs/hc-<random>`.

Wallet code: `HANDCASH-DESKTOP/src/wallet/logShip.ts`, `logUploadPrefs.ts`.
Server: `BRC-CLOUD/src/logs.js`.
